<section id="word-images">
					<section>
						<h1>Images</h1>
					</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Provide text alternative when needed</h2>
						<ul>
                			<li><strong>Informative image</strong>: provide text alternative</li>
                <li><strong>Decorative image</strong>: mark as decorative</li>
                <li><strong>Complex image</strong>: Provide short text alternative + complete visible text version
                	</li>
            		</ul>

					</section>

					<section>
						<h2>Provide an alternate text for images that convey information</h2>
						<ul>
							<li>Picture format > alt text</li>
							<li>Or right click on image > View alt text</li>
						</ul>
						<p><img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/applications/Word365/format_image_alt.jpg" alt=""></p>

					</section>

					<section>
						<img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/applications/Word365/alt_text.png" alt="alt text dialog window">

					</section>

					<section>
						<h2>Option 1 : provide alt text</h2>
						<ul>
							<li>Should be a good replacement for the image</li>
							<li>Concise</li>
							<li>Rather convey info than describe image in details</li>

						</ul>
					</section>

					<section>
						<h2>Option 2 : Mark image as decorative</h2>
						<ul>
							<li>If image doesn't convey information, mark as decorative</li>
							<li>OK if document remains understandable and complete without the image</li>
							<li>Tip : Make image decorative by providing same info in text</li>
							<li>Also possible for Word shapes</li>
						</ul>
					</section>

										<section>
						<h2>Option 3 : Generate alt text (AI)</h2>
						<ul>
							<li>Avoid doing this!</li>
							<li>Generally too long</li>
							<li>Doesn't take context into account</li>

						</ul>
					</section>

					<section>
						<h2>Complex image</h2>
						<ul>
							<li>Provide a concise text alternative via alt text field</li>
							<li>Also provide an extensive visible text alternative. </li>

						</ul>
					</section>

					<section>
						<h2>Avoid images of text</h2>
						<p>Less readable than real text</p>
					</section>

					<section>
						<h2>Image placement</h2>
						<ul>
							<li>Avoid floating images (with text wrapping)</li>
							<li>Place image inline, unless it is decorative</li>
						</ul>

					</section>

					<section>
						<img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/applications/Word365/inline_image.png" alt="">
					</section>

					<section>
						<h2>Exercise : images </h2>
						<ol>
							<li>Start from the result of the previous exercise</li>
